WEBVTT

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:06.340
Today's practice went pretty well, didn't it?

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:10.650
Yeah, but I think there's still 
a lot of room for improvement.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:12.740
We're still growing, in other words!

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.350
That's true.

00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:15.970
I like that way of thinking!

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:18.120
It's no fun if you just think you can't do it.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.090
Huh? We're out of shampoo?

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.210
Oh, you can use mine.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:24.620
Thanks, Tsubame-chin!

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.380
I'll give you some of my conditioner, then!

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:30.340
Your hair will be super shiny if you use this.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:32.090
What? Really?

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:33.920
Give me some, too!

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.640
Wow, this smells like melon.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.550
Io-chin uses the same kind!

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.240
We went shopping together.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.680
Want to try it, Satoka?

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:47.060
This really does smell like melon.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.370
I want to use yours, Io-chin!

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:53.080
Huh? We have the same kind.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.130
That's not what I mean!

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:03.060
We detected a signature in Sector S 
that doesn't match a normal O'bli.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.870
It could just be dimensional noise,

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:08.250
but I would like you all to investigate.

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:10.120
Roger.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:13.880
Altair Torte will proceed to 
coordinates 2-3-8 and investigate.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:15.840
Thank you.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.720
She's really acting like a leader now.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:22.770
A "realeader," for short.

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:23.920
How reliable.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:25.520
Yeah.

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:32.530
Here I go.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:40.890
Take that!

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:44.790
There!

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:49.000
Hey.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:55.330
Wow!

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:56.620
How pretty!

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:01.740
The dimensional signature 
was coming from this area.

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:05.320
Echo!

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:12.420
Echo, echo...

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:12.960
Io-chin, you're so nice!

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:15.720
I see.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:19.970
That's why we have a swimsuit Memoca...
Because there are places like this.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:21.190
That's right!

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:23.800
I get to see Io-chin in a swimsuit!

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:27.360
Mana-chan, we didn't come here to play.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:28.180
I know!

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:31.850
We came to look for O'bli out here in nature!

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:35.170
I don't think you'll find any under there.

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:35.840
Huh?

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:38.690
No, it's possible there's an ant-type O'bli.

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:39.500
Yeah.

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:41.520
Or an earthworm-type.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:42.920
We'll have to dig!

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:45.990
Let's take a look around first.

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:19.290
<b>Raid! SF Super Plan</b>

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:19.290
Wow, look at this!

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:21.610
It's a treasure trove of ingredients!

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:23.370
Wow, wow, wow!

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:27.360
I need to get Cuisenaire 
Sajima-san and have him

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:30.540
prepare a full course using 
ingredients from the mountain!

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:31.260
Yeah!

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:34.640
That's quite the attractive suggestion.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:35.770
Yeah!

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:37.420
For example...

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:39.150
For example? For example?

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:44.860
Uh-oh.

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:46.850
I, uh...

00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:49.380
Mana-chan, we didn't come here to play.

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:50.530
I know.

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:51.800
I'll do a good job.

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:53.920
The appetizer will be a matsutake salad.

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:56.300
The soup will be a Japanese yam vichyssoise.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:59.330
The main dish will be a pheasant 
saute with wild strawberry sauce.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:00.840
I see, I see.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:01.460
The desert will be a mountain grape mousse.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:02.580
Sounds delicious!

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:04.420
Okay, that's enough.

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:06.380
We didn't come here to go hiking.

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:08.370
O'bli-chin, come out!

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:09.390
Hey, hey!

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.270
Calling him out won't help.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.910
Oh...

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:19.240
But we can go gather ingredients 
once the mission's over, right?

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.320
Oh, all right.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:25.840
Once we're done.

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:27.380
Yay!

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:27.380
Echo!

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:28.540
All right, everyone!

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:31.160
Let's get this mission done!

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:35.950
Okay, we're going to check out this lake next.

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:38.600
That means...

00:06:41.390 --> 00:06:44.260
It's the changing-into-swimsuits 
segment we've been waiting for!

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:45.460
Right!

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:51.750
I wonder what kinds of fish are in a 
wonderful mountain lake like this one.

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:54.930
I wonder how many people we could 
feed if we caught a really big one.

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:56.560
Yuumi, Satoka.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:58.390
Yes, we know.

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:00.640
Only after we finish the mission.

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:14.420
Oh, how cute!

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:16.200
These are supposed to be for combat!

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:19.110
Wearing stuff like this is not my thing...

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:21.390
It's so cute, though.

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:23.880
Way to go, Tsubame-chan.

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:24.690
Huh?

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:26.890
Oh, Tsubame-san, your string.

00:07:26.890 --> 00:07:27.650
Huh?

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:41.970
Io-chin, you're the best!

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:43.570
Io-chin! Pant, pant...

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:45.060
Stop that. It's embarrassing.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:46.420
Drool, drool...

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:49.130
You have nothing to be embarrassed about!

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:52.100
Your body is perfect!

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:54.450
Hey, come on...

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:57.190
Yes! You all look cute!

00:07:57.190 --> 00:07:58.760
They suit you well!

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:00.120
Let's hurry.

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:01.930
Splash.

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:05.670
Here I go!

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:36.070
I'm tired.

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:37.820
I'm hungry.

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:39.580
Hungrys.

00:08:41.470 --> 00:08:44.580
Yes, we were unable to find the O'bli.

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:47.810
<i>We haven't detected anything since then,</i>

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:49.910
<i>so it could have just been noise.</i>

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:51.840
<i>Please head back, then.</i>

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:52.570
Okay.

00:08:52.570 --> 00:08:54.640
Hey, is the mission over?

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:55.970
Yes, I know.

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:02.390
Uh, would it be possible for us to take 
a break here before we head back?

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:06.260
<i>Sure.</i>

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:07.150
Really?

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:10.370
<i>It's a nice place.</i>

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:13.150
<i>I've been there before, too.</i>

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:16.970
<i>But it's possible an O'bli might still show up,</i>

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:18.390
<i>so please be careful.</i>

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:20.020
Understood.

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:22.130
Yay!

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:24.120
Let's go gather ingredients!

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:26.170
Okay, I'm gonna go fishing!

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:28.320
Huh? You brought that with you?

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:30.320
It came with the Memoca's equipment.

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:31.540
Oh...

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:33.910
I got this with mine.

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:34.600
Huh?

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:36.590
Okay, let's go!

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:39.550
Huh?

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:41.350
Fantastic!

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:43.270
With this many ingredients here,

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:46.810
Cuisenaire Sajima-san is 
going to be thrilled!

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:48.900
Oh! So it's finally time?

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:50.820
Of course.

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:53.360
Time to come to Japan.

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:57.860
Io-chin, did you catch any?

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:02.080
You're the one who brought up the idea,
and you're making me do it?

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:04.120
Well, there's nothing to catch here.

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:05.370
Really?

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:12.540
See?

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:16.760
I'm gonna catch one, too! A big one!

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:18.180
Give me that!

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:21.930
Thank you for waiting.

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:27.360
Here to make our special lunch 
today is Cuisenaire Sajima-san!

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:28.340
Applause!

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:30.300
Clap, clap, clap, clap.

00:10:31.410 --> 00:10:32.860
Hi, there!

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:38.740
Wrapping your knife in a scarf

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:40.560
and setting off on a journey

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:42.370
is très bien!

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:46.310
The wandering student of 
Japanese-style French cuisine,

00:10:46.310 --> 00:10:50.710
celebrity chef Cuisenaire 
Sajima-san's special lunch!

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:54.880
Bonjour, mademoiselle.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:58.510
A full course made with mountain ingredients!

00:10:58.510 --> 00:11:00.500
Wow, that looks good!

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:02.030
Pretty impressive, Yuumi.

00:11:02.030 --> 00:11:03.100
Non, non, non.

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:05.690
I am not Yuumi-san.

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:07.340
Many people confuse me for her.

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:08.930
What? It's really you?!

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:10.780
You're so trusting, Mana.

00:11:10.780 --> 00:11:13.080
You even brought plates?

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:15.970
I've made no oversights.

00:11:15.970 --> 00:11:18.040
You do good work.

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:19.520
But you're Yuumi, right?

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:20.610
Non, non, non.

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:23.190
I am not Yuumi-san.

00:11:23.190 --> 00:11:24.740
But you're Yuumi, right?

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:25.690
Non, non, non.

00:11:25.690 --> 00:11:26.990
I am...

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:29.000
Time to eat.

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:31.520
The fruit is so good.

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:32.890
The fish is good, too.

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:34.530
Really?! I'm so glad!

00:11:34.530 --> 00:11:36.210
Yuumi, you're back to normal.

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:38.510
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:50.480
So Sajima-san was here?

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:52.680
You're going to keep pushing that?

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:54.160
What are you talking about?

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:56.730
I wanted to see Sajima-san, though.

00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:00.160
Hey, where's Mana-chan?

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:01.610
She left not long ago to fish.

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:05.250
<i>Mana, we don't need fish anymore.</i>

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:07.460
But you caught all of them earlier.

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:09.540
I haven't caught any.

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:11.520
<i>I swear I'll catch one!</i>

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:14.410
Mana-chan doesn't like losing, huh?

00:12:14.410 --> 00:12:16.000
She doesn't look it, but...

00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:17.000
Here I go.

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:19.160
Huh? You're going to eat more?

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:21.310
Curry bread goes to a different stomach.

00:12:21.310 --> 00:12:25.860
Curry bread is a miracle super food that was 
created at the beginning of the Showa Era,

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:29.640
a mix of Western bread and Indian curry.

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:32.960
I always have room in my 
stomach for curry bre—

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:40.440
Wait!

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:41.600
Wait!

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:43.570
Wait!

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:45.910
My curry bread...

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:48.370
My curry bread!

00:12:59.130 --> 00:12:59.830
Whoa!

00:12:59.830 --> 00:13:00.690
A fish?!

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:01.780
A huge fish!

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:03.340
My curry bread!

00:13:15.030 --> 00:13:16.640
That's not a fish!

00:13:16.640 --> 00:13:18.260
It's a big fish O'bli.

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:20.110
Yukako-sensei!

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:21.220
Why are you here?

00:13:21.220 --> 00:13:23.240
You don't need to worry about that.

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:25.850
In any case, that's a rare O'bli.

00:13:25.850 --> 00:13:27.420
A big fish O'bli.

00:13:27.420 --> 00:13:29.520
We can't let it go.

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:30.660
Also, Yuumi-san!

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:31.900
Me?

00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:34.130
Call me "Tierra" during your missions.

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:35.700
Remember, this is a mission.

00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:36.740
Yes, ma'am.

00:13:36.740 --> 00:13:39.330
Okay, take care of it.

00:13:41.060 --> 00:13:42.380
She's gone already!

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:44.690
Mana-san!

00:13:44.690 --> 00:13:45.550
What's wrong?

00:13:46.020 --> 00:13:48.040
I think I hooked it!

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:54.950
When did the fishing line get that long—

00:13:54.170 --> 00:13:55.410
No! You can't ask about that!

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:56.520
Mana-chan!

00:13:57.860 --> 00:13:59.980
Calm down and listen, Mana!

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:01.720
Try letting go of the fishing rod!

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:05.160
No! I'm so scared, I can't let go!

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:06.030
What should we...

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:08.540
What should we do?

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:10.280
Leave it to us.

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:10.660
Huh?

00:14:11.060 --> 00:14:11.910
That's...

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:18.870
<b>Coconut Vega 
The Big One</b>

00:14:31.700 --> 00:14:33.570
It's everyone from Coconut Vega!

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:34.810
Why are they in a fishing boat?

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:39.480
Oh, they're encountering rough 
waves because of the O'bli.

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:42.100
Things have gotten pretty exciting.

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:42.740
Ako!

00:14:42.740 --> 00:14:43.520
Yep!

00:14:55.820 --> 00:14:56.620
I get it.

00:14:56.620 --> 00:15:00.080
They're using the barrels to slow 
it down as much as they can.

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:02.320
They're trying to save Mana.

00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:04.210
Way to go, Coconut Vega.

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:06.370
Where did they get that boat and the equipme—

00:15:07.530 --> 00:15:08.340
Do it now, Mari!

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:09.930
Got it.

00:15:15.730 --> 00:15:17.090
All right, let's get to it!

00:15:17.090 --> 00:15:17.680
Okay!

00:15:42.760 --> 00:15:43.680
Mana.

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:45.960
Io-chin...

00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:47.500
Thank goodness.

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:48.760
Thank you so much.

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:51.590
Sorry for causing such trouble all the time.

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:52.220
It's fine.

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:54.250
No big deal.

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:56.790
I'm supposed to be the leader, 
but I wasn't attentive enough.

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:58.690
I let my guard down, too.

00:15:58.690 --> 00:16:00.120
Me too, I guess.

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:02.170
I was fishing...

00:16:02.170 --> 00:16:03.400
My curry bread...

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:08.240
In any case, I'm glad Mana's okay.

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:09.750
As long as we're in the barrier,

00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:13.450
remember there's always the 
danger of an O'bli showing up.

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:16.370
The mission isn't over until you're back home.

00:16:17.510 --> 00:16:18.540
Right.

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:21.120
All right, you can get all depressed later.

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:23.790
No point in dwelling on your mistakes.

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:24.780
Right.

00:16:24.780 --> 00:16:25.600
Good.

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:28.940
Now, there is a way to fix your
mistake. Want to hear it?

00:16:28.940 --> 00:16:29.460
Sure.

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:33.330
We might be able to win if we team up.

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:34.180
You're right.

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:36.280
Two heads are better than one.

00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:36.990
Huh?

00:16:36.990 --> 00:16:37.640
What?

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:39.490
Time for a joint planning session.

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:43.460
<b>Five Dimensional Lake, Above the Jump Platform</b>

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:45.650
<b>Altair Torte</b>

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:45.650
<b>Altair Torte Special Tent</b>

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:49.360
Combining the witness statements 
from both Vega and Torte,

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.230
<b>Altair Torte</b>

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.230
<b>Coconut Vega</b>

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:49.360
<b>First Conference for the Mission 
to Eliminate the Unknown Creature</b>

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:51.270
we know the big O'bli is a fish-type.

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:54.490
<b>Coconut Vega 
Takamine Ako</b>

00:16:51.270 --> 00:16:54.660
These abnormal O'bli take a fixed shape 
and inherit their properties,

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:57.320
so we can consider this O'bli water-based.

00:16:57.320 --> 00:17:00.740
That means it's still in the lake somewhere.

00:16:57.370 --> 00:17:00.740
<b>Coconut Vega 
Ibuki Imina</b>

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:03.180
We can't attack it when it's underwater.

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:05.870
<b>Coconut Vega 
Shiranui Hazuki</b>

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:05.870
We need to lure it out somehow.

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:06.920
What should we do?

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:07.330
<b>Coconut Vega 
Shinonome Ryouko</b>

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:07.680
I know!

00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:13.550
<b>Altair Torte 
Namori Mana</b>

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:09.470
I have a good idea!

00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:10.180
What is it?

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:11.760
How about we fish it up?

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:13.550
It did take my bait earlier.

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:18.800
<b>Coconut Vega 
Yukishiro Mari</b>

00:17:13.940 --> 00:17:16.290
So we all put out lines, then?

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:18.800
We can't pull in something that big.

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:22.200
I guess that was too simple.

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:22.770
No...

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:24.030
It might work.

00:17:22.830 --> 00:17:25.270
<b>Altair Torte 
Sumihara Satoka</b>

00:17:24.030 --> 00:17:25.270
Huh?

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:33.400
Are you sure about this?

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:37.250
You're willing to go along 
with such a crazy plan?

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:40.120
I went along with it because 
it sounded interesting.

00:17:40.590 --> 00:17:41.870
You're all the same, right?

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:43.580
<i>No problem here.</i>

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:47.170
Satokacchi and I have an obscene 
give-and-take relationship.

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:51.290
We have no such thing!

00:17:51.290 --> 00:17:52.880
<i>Don't say stuff like that!</i>

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:56.050
I'm just happy I get to be on the 
same mission as you, Yuumi.

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:57.800
We're on different teams, so I didn't 
think we'd get to do anything together.

00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:59.790
<i>We're on different teams, so I didn't 
think we'd get to do anything together.</i>

00:18:00.740 --> 00:18:02.640
I'm happy too, Ryouko-chan.

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:05.760
We're friends with the same goal in mind.

00:18:05.760 --> 00:18:07.600
Of course we'll help you out.

00:18:07.910 --> 00:18:09.020
<i>Right, Mari?</i>

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:09.870
Whatever.

00:18:09.870 --> 00:18:11.250
I just follow orders.

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:12.940
That was kind of cool!

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:19.410
<b>Big one</b>

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:19.410
<b>Fifth Dimensional Lake Map</b>

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:16.500
Judging from its escape route,

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:19.410
it normally inhabits the left size of the lake.

00:18:19.900 --> 00:18:22.260
We'll drive it to the right 
by attacking on three sides.

00:18:22.260 --> 00:18:23.870
I understand that,

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:25.970
but can we really catch it that way?

00:18:23.930 --> 00:18:25.970
<b>Altair Torte 
Sajima Yuumi</b>

00:18:26.240 --> 00:18:29.040
<i>I got it totally by chance earlier.</i>

00:18:29.410 --> 00:18:31.140
You have some secret plan, right?

00:18:31.140 --> 00:18:31.540
Yes.

00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:33.380
Right here.

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:33.380
<b>Curry Bread</b>

00:18:33.580 --> 00:18:34.970
Curry bread?

00:18:34.970 --> 00:18:36.880
When I dropped that curry bread,

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:38.840
the big one showed up.

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:40.280
The way it bit down...

00:18:40.280 --> 00:18:42.320
It likes curry bread for sure.

00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:43.420
Are you sure of that?

00:18:43.420 --> 00:18:45.810
Yes. I like curry bread, so I can tell.

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:47.860
We're going to use this as bait.

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:50.810
<b>Altair Torte 
Miyama Tsubame</b>

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:49.130
Are you sure?

00:18:49.130 --> 00:18:50.810
You love curry bread...

00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:53.310
I'm a member of Altair Torte, as well.

00:18:53.590 --> 00:18:57.030
I've wanted to repay Vega for all they've done.

00:18:58.170 --> 00:18:59.280
Thanks, Satoka.

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:01.780
Got it.

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:05.110
Let's try this plan, then.

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:10.370
<b>Unknown Creature</b>

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:11.300
Now!

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:13.210
Start the strike fishing plan!

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:16.710
Roger!

00:19:24.710 --> 00:19:28.390
<i>Altair Torte, the O'bli is heading 
toward the planned fishing spot.</i>

00:19:28.820 --> 00:19:30.850
<i>Prepare to intercept it for us!</i>

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:45.830
<i>10,000 until the O'bli hits the fishing spot.</i>

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:52.440
Satoka.

00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:55.540
The O'bli is coming.

00:19:57.060 --> 00:19:58.300
What will you do, Satoka?

00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:09.470
5,000 until the O'bli 
reaches the designated spot.

00:20:20.600 --> 00:20:21.460
Right.

00:20:22.020 --> 00:20:23.990
<i>3,000 until the designated spot.</i>

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:33.830
<i>1,500 until the designated spot.</i>

00:20:35.840 --> 00:20:37.560
<i>800 until the designated spot.</i>

00:20:40.180 --> 00:20:43.470
Get that O'bli!

00:20:42.660 --> 00:20:43.470
<i>500.</i>

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:44.900
<i>400.</i>

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:45.930
<i>300.</i>

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:47.510
<i>200.</i>

00:20:48.160 --> 00:20:49.130
<i>100.</i>

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:52.770
Goodbye, curry bread.

00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:59.900
<b>Five Dimensional Lake 
Mana Satoka 
550 metric tons 
57 meters 
Big Fish O'bli</b>

00:20:57.840 --> 00:20:58.640
Huh?

00:20:58.640 --> 00:20:59.900
You fished it up?

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:02.790
Oh, you mean the big fish O'bli.

00:21:02.790 --> 00:21:03.740
Good work.

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:06.550
What's up, moshu?

00:21:06.550 --> 00:21:10.320
Torte and Coconut are fishing 
with curry, supposedly.

00:21:11.140 --> 00:21:12.750
I don't understand, moshu.

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:21.000
They're growing every day.

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:24.630
I wonder if it was okay to take this picture.

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:26.790
That's what you do when you catch a fish.

00:21:26.790 --> 00:21:27.680
Yeah.

00:21:28.130 --> 00:21:29.280
Why not?

00:21:29.280 --> 00:21:31.680
That way we won't forget what we learned.

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:33.270
Proof that we fought.

00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:35.980
Yeah.

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:40.980
<b>Clash! The Two Formidable Enemies</b>

00:23:37.860 --> 00:23:40.470
"Clash! The Two Formidable Enemies."
